Looking at this problem, I need to determine whether the hyperoctahedral group $G = S_2 \wr S_n = (\mathbb{Z}/2)^n \rtimes S_n$ has exactly 3 maximal normal subgroups, or whether there are additional ones beyond the three described.

**Answer Leak Check:** The problem describes three known index-2 normal subgroups and asks if there are more. It does not reveal the answer or proof strategy. No leak detected.

